## Context (recorded, never gated)

- Per-conjunct raw counts: C1 (weighted top block omits `b*`) 6/30 · C2 (unweighted top block covers `b*`) 29/30 · C3 (counterfactual top block covers `b*`) 28/30; all three together 4/30.
- C2 is entailed by the sanity leg (`b*` is a required bit, so a top block covering ALL of `required` covers `b*`), so on a valid run the skip leg is effectively C1 ∧ C3.
- A skip-leg shortfall decomposes into "no flip" (¬C1) and "control failed" (C1 ∧ C3 missing, i.e. C1 ∧ C2 ∧ ¬C3), the latter measured on 1/30 seeds. A control failure is a SIZE effect of the uniform counterfactual — scaling every reliability to 0.35 scales the coverage terms but not the `8`-per-member cost — and is not evidence about routing.
- **Attribution validity:** `W̄`'s and `U`'s argmax partitions differ on 27/30 seeds. Expected 0 — at a uniform reliability the weighted total is an increasing affine map of the unweighted total, so the two argmaxes coincide up to float ties. Any nonzero count means C1-vs-C3 was an intent-to-treat contrast across DIFFERENT partitions on those seeds. Counted, never asserted, so a float tie cannot panic the registered run.
- The weighted and unweighted argmax **partitions** differ at all on 28/30 seeds. Member costs sum to the partition-constant −8·N under every calculator here, so member savings can never motivate a partition change; any difference counted here comes from the coverage terms alone.
- Coverage-guaranteed draw: 2 instance re-draws across the 30 seeds (the #61 draw had no guarantee and missed coverage on 5/30).
- Leg C degeneracy: all-singletons ties or beats the argmax on 30/30 (bar 15) → **DEGENERATE (context only)**; the argmax IS all-singletons on 0/30 and the grand coalition ties-or-beats it on 0/30.


