## VERDICT: **FALSIFIED (process structure)**

_Grammar (prereg §7): `VALIDATED (process structure)` = at least one H-P cell passes BOTH conjuncts at the family-wise bar with every §6 gate holding · `FALSIFIED (process structure)` = gates hold, no cell clears the bar · `RUN-INVALID` = any §6 gate fails. This run: carrying cell none · gates X-reduce PASS / S-sound PASS / S-dedup PASS. E-ceil / E-conc / E-fuel mechanism-scoping is reported below but cannot upgrade the verdict. **Scope of a `VALIDATED` reading (Amendment A5.1, binding):** it would read "**a sound-by-stipulation process transformation can unlock staffing value in this world**" — the rewrite rules are hand-authored for this experiment and BGKSZ Thm 5.6 certifies only that the optimizer stayed inside them, so the claim is NOT "process reorganisation is generically valuable". The v1/v2 K4 verdicts, EQ3's and EQ4's verdicts, and the #54 arm question (mag = demonstrated default, FINAL) are UNTOUCHED regardless of outcome, and a `VALIDATED` result would speak to the process-vs-as-written contrast within the typed magnitude family — not to the mag-vs-aif arm question, which is EQ5b's (prereg §7 pre-commitments)._

