## H-PS (confirmatory — BOTH conjuncts required, prereg §4)

- **Conjunct 1 — FAIL.** `lift_w = r_w − 1`: `lift_wf` **+0.3355**, `lift_flat` **+0.3355** (`r_flat` 1.3355×). Bar: `lift_wf ≥ 1.25 × max(lift_flat, 0)` = **0.4194**. **The floor is load-bearing** (#80 formalism pin): a raw `lift_wf / lift_flat` blows up as `lift_flat → 0` and FLIPS SIGN when the lever hurts on flat, which would let a mediocre `res-wf` pass on a negative denominator. Flooring at 0 also means that if the lever does nothing on flat, any positive workflow lift satisfies this conjunct — which is *correct* (no flat lift ⇒ process-specific) and is exactly why S-repl carries the "and the effect is real" half.
  - **Floor condition (Amendment A1.2/A1.3): contested.** `lift_flat` is measured and positive (+0.3355), so `bar_c1` = **0.4194** is a real bar and conjunct 1 is a **contested** test — both conjuncts are doing discriminating work.
- **Conjunct 2 — FAIL.** Paired per-seed `margin_wf > margin_flat` on **0/30** seeds against the bar **18**, where `margin_w` = per-seed PRIMARY(`res-w`) − PRIMARY(`ctl-w`) — a **difference, not a ratio**, because differences are well-behaved at zero. Exact ties (`margin_wf == margin_flat`, i.e. the residual weighting made no difference at all on that seed): **30**; a tie is not a win and counts against the bar, which is the honest reading on a seed whose writing repeats nothing.
