# koalisi #78 — Part 11: the typed two-engine contest (REGISTERED)

_governed by `docs/prereg-K4-eq5b-typed-two-engine.md` **including Amendments 1–5** (committed BEFORE this code; design-lock of record [koalisi #78](https://github.com/sustia-llc/koalisi/issues/78)). Report date 2026-08-08. Seeds **330..360** (fresh; 90..120 and 150..180 stay reserved). **H-G (confirmatory):** an active-inference engine deciding over role-restricted coverage queries — `aif::GroupAgent`, R ≤ 3 role internals over arm-E1's persistent world model, `CertaintyWeighted` active slot, `n_actions = 2` — beats the EQ4-validated typed magnitude arm staffing the same workflows. The control is that validated arm, so EQ5b cannot re-harvest EQ4's margin._

_**READ THIS BEFORE THE TABLE — Amendment A5.1, the review's central finding.** This arm is **not** "a group of role specialists deliberating about a candidate". It is **a group of role-restricted coverage queries, of which only the candidate's own role internal is candidate-sensitive; the remainder vote on their role's coalition coverage.** Under A2.1's registered role-matched masks the candidate's capabilities reach only its own role's internal, so for every other internal `cfg0 == cfg1` **exactly** on the leave path and the candidate appears in neither mask on the join path — measured, two candidates of a non-rostered role produce **bit-identical scores**. **And the blind internals do not abstain:** `run_replay` records control 0 before every observation, so only the membership-0 columns of `pA` accumulate, A-novelty rewards switching, and indifference resolves to `p(act) = 1.0` at **zero entropy — the MAXIMUM `CertaintyWeighted` weight**. A1.3's `[0.5, 0.5]`-at-weight-0.5 rationale is **WITHDRAWN as measurably false and inverted in sign**; its decision to drop empty-demand roles stands. **The arm is NOT re-specified**: restricting the roster to candidate-sensitive internals would force R = 1 on every decision, i.e. under role-matched masks a group deliberating about one candidate is structurally impossible — and that IS the finding. It is disclosed and measured below, per cell._

_**Amendment 1**: the arm as first registered was unbuildable — SP1's arm-E1 query construction bakes the per-decision candidate into each member's matrices, while `POMDPAgent` exposes no setter for `A`/`B`/`C`/`D` and `GroupAgent` no way to replace a member, so D2a's "persistent internals" and SP1 were mutually exclusive. A1.1 relocates D2a's contrast from member continuity to **world-model topology**: confirmatory cells own **R = 3 role-specialised** persistent models, the reference cells read **one shared** model through three role-restricted views. Members are single-use on every leg, **D4a is struck** (there is nothing for a commit to advance), and the MMP double-update hazard of gotcha 32 is DESIGNED OUT rather than gated — which is why S-learn below is thinner than the 2026-08-08 correction described. **Amendment 2**: the coverage masks are registered **role-matched** (the world's own `p9_step_covered` is role-matched), with `grp-role-blind` as a single non-gating reference isolating that mechanism, and SP3 applies **uniformly to join and leave** — this arm declines on a tie where arm-E1 leaves on one._

_**Amendment 3**, made with off-block smoke visible and recorded as such: D2 pinned `CertaintyWeighted` as **forced** because only it was thought to carry a continuous margin at R ≤ 3 over 2 actions. **That premise is measured false on this world** — the E-agree margin median sits at 0.5, so the mixture is itself a delta and SP3's threshold is never contested. Two sources, and **A5.1 corrects which dominates**: the group propagates arm-E1's inherited gotcha-25 saturation **and adds a second source** — an internal whose two coverage configurations are identical is not undecided but maximally confident for "act" — and **on this roster the second source is the larger one**. **The confirmatory cells are NOT re-specified** (post-hoc instrument re-targeting, refused at EQ5a A5.2); the cost is MEASURED by the non-gating `grp-role-det` leg. **Amendment 4** replaces A3.1's expectation that `grp-role-det` would land near `grp-role`: saturated *members* do not make a confidence-weighted mixture and a winner-set vote agree, because CW weights by `exp(−H)` while the tally is one-member-one-vote — which at R = 2 makes SP3 a **unanimity** rule. A3.2 promotes a `grp-mult` vs `grp-role` act-and-score-bit line to a **mandatory** disclosure._

_**Amendment 5 — the 3-lens review**: five blocking, ~15 important, ~30 minor findings, every one dispositioned. Beyond A5.1 above: **A5.2** adds a pre-committed scoped claim against `arm-E1`, the single-agent shape of the very engine this wraps, recorded at 1.62× magnitude in v5 and run here on identical instances. **A5.3** implements S-learn (iii) as the non-gating `grp-role-nonov` cell. **A5.4** repairs S-learn (i): the tolerance is prereg-pinned at 1e-9, `expected` is re-derived independently from the task stream so a **surplus** is reachable at all, and the non-vacuity guard is per-model `all` rather than `any`. **A5.5** relabels S-live a disclosure — as implemented it cannot fail. **A5.6** corrects the `Deterministic` read to uniform-over-winners `{0, 0.5, 1}`. **A5.7** withdraws A2.3's "purely": with novelty off the read still moves (`0.500000000 → 0.500002287`), because `update_a` re-derives `A` after an unscaled `η·joint`, so SP2 moves concentration **predominantly**, not purely. **A5.8**: SP2's registered sign is **BACKWARDS** — concentration is evidence **possessed**, so higher multiplicity means **less** epistemic pull, and a repeated step makes the arm markedly **less** willing to staff it (`p(act)` `0.999999991 → 0.501759150` as `m` goes 1 → 3); the word "demand" is withdrawn and the mechanism is unchanged. **A5.9**: "changes the engine, not the criterion" is narrowed — three things differ from arm-E1, so EQ5b changes the engine **and the aggregation**, and only the threshold is held fixed._

_**Smoke disclosure (A5.10 L2-20), stated plainly rather than as an aside:** Amendments 3, 4 and 5 were all written with off-block smoke showing the confirmatory cell **apparently passing** — `grp-role` at 1.379× on 2 seeds, above conjunct 1's bar. None of them moves the bar, adds a confirmatory cell, or re-specifies the arm; the reader is entitled to know they were made with a favourable number visible._

## Gates (prereg §5 — any failure ⇒ `RUN-INVALID`)

_**Two senses of "gating", separated (Amendment A5.10 L2-5).** A **validity-gating** item is one whose failure makes the run `RUN-INVALID`: the four below. A **verdict-gating** item is one that can change the verdict *label*: only H-G, in a confirmatory cell, against the bar D6 fixed at lock time. No non-gating leg can move either, and the bar cannot be relitigated after the numbers are visible._

- **X-identity — PASS.** At the identity configuration `m ≡ 1` the multiplicity channel reproduces its base **bit-identically on acts and raw score bits** (and on per-seed PRIMARY bits and churn), all 30 seeds: role-specialised PASS · shared PASS (A5.10 L2-19 — the gate covered only the confirmatory pair before). Asked on the all-parallel degenerate world, which carries `m ≡ 1` everywhere and consumes ZERO extra stream draws, so its base prefix is bit-for-bit the v2w instance of the same seed. This is what keeps SP2 from being a free parameter — the scale is `m(b, r)` or it is nothing.
  - **Scale alignment — PASS** (A5.10 L2-16). An SP2 scale vector permuted against the query's modality order is invisible to the identity above, because every entry is 1 there. Checked directly: with per-bit multiplicities that differ, swapping which bit carries which must move the read, and it does.
- **S-determinism — PASS.** Every **model** cell re-run from scratch and compared per seed on acts, raw score bits, PRIMARY bits and churn: `grp-role` 30/30 · `grp-mult` 30/30 · `grp-role-shared` 30/30 · `grp-mult-shared` 30/30 · `grp-role-blind` 30/30 · `grp-role-nonov` 30/30. Extended from the confirmatory pair to all five (A5.10 L2-3), since A4.2 gates model-variations.
  - **Seed invariance — PASS** (30/30). Reproducibility alone would be passed by a seeded sampler, so the real claim is that the deterministic read consumes no randomness at all: re-running `grp-role` with a **different** `battery_seed` must reproduce it bit-for-bit. Valid because the seed reaches the engine only as `AgentParams { seed }` — the world models, the per-decision query seed, the `VotingAgent` and the group RNG. (A5.10 L2-4 struck the old rationale, which claimed a slip to `act` would surface here; the `grp-seed` cell in this very run refutes that.)
- **S-learn (i) — PASS.** Per seed, each world model must record **exactly one** update per task in which its role had demand — **counted, not inferred from state movement**, because under MMP a missing commit makes an update apply TWICE rather than not at all, so "did the state move?" passes a double-updating arm. Deficit and surplus are both `RUN-INVALID`. Seeds with an exact ledger, and seeds whose every **in-scope** world model moved off initialization by more than 1e-9 (the prereg-pinned non-vacuity tolerance — necessary, explicitly NOT sufficient): `grp-role` 30/30 exact, 30/30 moved · `grp-mult` 30/30 exact, 30/30 moved · `grp-role-shared` 30/30 exact, 30/30 moved · `grp-mult-shared` 30/30 exact, 30/30 moved · `grp-role-blind` 30/30 exact, 30/30 moved · `grp-role-nonov` 30/30 exact, 30/30 moved · `grp-role-det` (reported, not gated) 30/30 exact, 30/30 moved · `grp-seed` (reported, not gated) 30/30 exact, 30/30 moved. **Amendment A6.1 scopes non-vacuity to models with `expected > 0`.** The first official run (`7e265fe`) returned `RUN-INVALID` here with the counted ledger 30/30 exact on every cell: seeds **354** and **355** each carried a role model at `expected == 0, updates == 0, max |pA delta| == 0e0` — never asked to learn, because `p8_task_feasible` requires a pool worker **of the tagged role** holding each required bit, so a role absent from the pool can never be legally tagged (354 is `n = 5` with worker-role counts `[3, 0, 2]`; 355 is `n = 4` with `[2, 0, 2]`). At `P(role absent) = 3·(2/3)^n − 3·(1/3)^n` — 0.553 at `n = 4`, 12.5 % of seeds, ≈ 3.76 expected failures per 30-seed block — **no seed block passes the uncorrected guard**, so the guard is what changed and not the block. **Exempt models, disclosed per cell and per seed:** `grp-role` 2 model(s) on 2/30 seeds — (354, r1), (355, r1) · `grp-mult` 2 model(s) on 2/30 seeds — (354, r1), (355, r1) · `grp-role-shared` none · `grp-mult-shared` none · `grp-role-blind` 2 model(s) on 2/30 seeds — (354, r1), (355, r1) · `grp-role-nonov` 2 model(s) on 2/30 seeds — (354, r1), (355, r1) · `grp-role-det` 2 model(s) on 2/30 seeds — (354, r1), (355, r1) · `grp-seed` 2 model(s) on 2/30 seeds — (354, r1), (355, r1). A5.4's `all` stands **within** that scope, so a model that WAS asked and stayed frozen still fails, and "everything exempt" is not a pass.
  - **Amendment A5.4 repaired two things here.** The tolerance is now **prereg-pinned** rather than a harness local that §5 twice described as registered. And `expected` is re-derived **independently from the task stream** — `begin_task` writes it, `observe_outcome` writes only `updates` — so a **surplus is reachable at all**: before, `expected` was incremented immediately beside the guarded `updates` on the same path, which made `updates > expected` impossible and the RUN-INVALID surplus condition near-tautological. The non-vacuity guard is per-model **`all`**, not `any`; under `RoleSpecialised` a role model that never moved used to pass because a sibling did.
  - `begin_task` rejections across the **gated** cells: **0** (read-probe cells, reported separately: 0). A rejection means the world names a role or a bit the arm is not configured for — a harness fault, and a **registered** RUN-INVALID condition since A5.10 L2-11, which also scoped this total to the cells it actually gates. **S-learn (ii) and the member-advance conjunct are STRUCK as vacuous** by A1.4: members are single-use on every leg and there is no commit on the decision path, so neither has a referent.
- **X-battery** (frozen Parts 1–10 byte-identical on every quality/ratio/superiority/churn/verdict line) is checked OUTSIDE this binary, by diffing this run's Parts 1–10 against a `main` baseline captured before HEAD is run; latency-only diffs are the standing exclusion. Part 11 is purely additive, and the one thing that could disturb it is the arm-E1 seam the group arm reuses: `build_query` gained an `Option<&[f64]>` count scale that is `None` on every pre-existing call site (the scaling block is skipped, not multiplied by one), and `observe_outcome` became a delegation to a flag-returning twin with an identical body. Structural, and still **owed** as a measurement.

