_**A1.3**: a role with no `(bit, role)` demand in a task does not vote in it — it leaves the roster, so the realised `R` varies 3 → 2 → 1. A task where EVERY role is empty cannot occur (`|required| ≥ 2`). **A1.3's original rationale is WITHDRAWN as measurably false (A5.1)**: it argued that an abstaining member reads `[0.5, 0.5]` at weight `exp(−ln 2) = 0.5` and would drag `p(act)` toward the threshold. A member with no candidate-discriminating coverage reads ≈ 1.0 at weight 1.0, and its bias is toward **act**, not toward the threshold — wrong in size and **inverted in sign**. The decision to drop empty-demand roles stands; the hazard was real and dropping is still right._
_**E-agree** reads each internal's own argmax back off the roster after the read — a disclosure, never a decision input — and is split by candidate-sensitivity in the A5.1 table above. The **votes and roster columns are commensurable across every cell**; the **margin column is not**: it is `|p(act) − 0.5|`, the CW mixture's distance from the threshold on CW cells and a **winner-set indicator** on `grp-role-det` (marked, A5.6). The seeded-sampling cell exposes no distribution and so records no sample at all. A margin median at 0.5 means the read is a delta and SP3's threshold is never contested — see Amendment 3, as corrected by A5.1 on which source dominates._

## S-live (DISCLOSURE, not a gate — Amendment A5.5)

- Divergence from `wf-asis`, reported as **acts AND raw score bits separately**: `grp-role` 30/30 seeds, 8948 acts, 11705 score bits · `grp-mult` 30/30 seeds, 8949 acts, 11699 score bits · `grp-role-shared` 30/30 seeds, 8827 acts, 11612 score bits · `grp-mult-shared` 30/30 seeds, 8825 acts, 11608 score bits · `grp-role-blind` 30/30 seeds, 9115 acts, 11861 score bits · `grp-role-nonov` 30/30 seeds, 7631 acts, 10936 score bits · `grp-role-det` 30/30 seeds, 8270 acts, 11117 score bits · `grp-seed` 30/30 seeds, 8848 acts, 11751 score bits. This is the #80 lesson (gotcha 31): a term can be live in the score and dead at the decision, and a leg reading only PRIMARY sees a flat null where the truth is "it reached the margin and never crossed a threshold". Read the two columns against each other before reading any median.
- **Why it is no longer listed as a gate.** As implemented it asks whether ≥ 1 of 30 seeds shows ≥ 1 differing act **versus a different engine** — not falsifiable in any realistic world, so presenting it under "any failure ⇒ RUN-INVALID" overstated the run's validity checking. The #80 lesson it cites is about a lever versus **its own base**, and the only such comparison here is A3.2's `grp-mult` vs `grp-role`, which the registration fixes as non-gating. Moved to the disclosures verbatim, with nothing about what it measures changed (A5.5).

