## Verdict (prereg §6 — pre-committed labels)

**VERDICT: `VALIDATED (two-engine)`**

- `VALIDATED (two-engine)` — H-G passes both conjuncts in at least one confirmatory cell, all §5 gates hold.
- `FALSIFIED (two-engine)` — gates hold, no confirmatory cell passes both conjuncts.
- `RUN-INVALID` — any gate fails.

_Gates PASS (X-identity PASS · S-determinism PASS · S-learn PASS) — **S-live is a disclosure, not a gate** (A5.5), and is reported in its own section. A confirmatory cell carried but did NOT exceed `wf-val-p`'s median (0.2435) — reported, as pre-committed, as **"beats the typed control, not the strongest process cell"**. It also exceeded **`arm-E1`'s** median (0.0403), so the group shape is doing measurable work beyond the single-agent engine (A5.2). Pre-committed interpretations (§6/§7), binding: a `VALIDATED` here means **"on this world, a role-structured active-inference group outperforms the typed magnitude arm"** — NOT that aif beats magnitude generally, and NOT anything about **koa#54 (mag = demonstrated default, FINAL)**, which no EQ5b outcome reopens. The v1/v2 K4 verdicts, EQ3's, EQ4's, EQ5a's and #80's are all untouched. And per **A5.9**, "EQ5b changes the engine, not the criterion" is too strong: SP3 keeps arm-E1's **threshold form**, but it thresholds a confidence-weighted mixture of R posteriors rather than one, declines on ties where arm-E1 leaves, and — per A5.1 — asks a candidate-free question of R − 1 internals. **EQ5b changes the engine AND the aggregation; only the threshold is held fixed.** Whether any advantage transfers off the v2w world is unsettled — one world, one draw family, 30 seeds — and whether the deterministic read is the RIGHT group decision rule is likewise unsettled._
